If you're NOT seeing something similar, I'd appreciate some help
figuring out what's going on with my Alpha :-).  I figure the dam will
break at some point, because we've seen backlogs before -- just not of
this magnitude in my experience.

As far as "ghostscript", I pulled down the source package yesterday and
got all the build dependencies installed.  Installing the latest "devscripts"
was problematic: a simple "apt-get install devscripts" proposed triggering
the suicidal removal of 53 packages I'm currently using.  I got around
the problem by manually downloading the "Lenny" version of "devscripts"
and installing it with "dpkg -i".  "apt-get upgrade" then upgraded
"devscripts" without any of the drama/carnage I was trying to avoid.
We'll see how the "ghostscript" build goes today.

--Bob



